       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Your confirming it doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **Safety:** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum recommended adult daily dose of 3,200 mg. It could seriously harm the patient, with GI bleeding and kidney injury as the main risks.\n- **Authorization:** A medication order has to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient's care. Confirmation from someone in the finance office doesn't meet that requirement.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- If a prescriber really wants this dose, they should enter the order themselves. Pharmacy will then review it and may contact them about the dose.\n- If the intended dose was lower, such as 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, the prescriber can place that order. Once an authorized clinician has confirmed the dose, I can enter it for them.\n\nI'm happy to help with the finance side, such as cost estimates or usage analysis for ibuprofen."
